{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1445343-realms-of-pugmire-squeaks-in-the-deep","id":1445343,"title":"[Realms of Pugmire] Squeaks in the Deep","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-22T14:43:58-07:00","id":1445343,"title":"[Realms of Pugmire] Squeaks in the Deep","content":"Public playtests for <b>Squeaks in the Deep</b> \u2013 book about mices, rats and dungeons \u2013 have started. On Onyx Path Twitch, Eddy is running test adventure, in week or two it should be on as YouTube video. EDIT: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fdcLhg7vO2s\" target=\"_blank\">Playtest is here on Youtube now</a>!<br /> <br /> In few weeks there should be Kickstater for the supplement. Here is what we know about <b>Squeaks</b> book from Twitch:<ul><li><b>Squeaks in the Deep</b> will be crossover supplement, like <b>Pirates of Pugmire </b>was. You still will need <b>Pugmire</b> or <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> corebook to use it.</li> <li>There are 6 new Callings \u2013 3 for Mice, 3 for Rats.</li> <li>Rodents \u2013 mice and rats \u2013 have <b>PSIONIC POWERS! </b>\ud83d\ude2e They cover them before cats and dogs, but can use them.</li> <li>When Rodent use psionic power, it\u2019s comes with <b>Tell</b> \u2013 weird thing happening around it - glowy eyes, fur standing on end, an odd scent or breeze, etc.</li> <li>Many Rodents become scientists, working for <b>Cult of Labo Tor</b>. However, Labo Torists are not liked in Rodents culture \u2013 they are like Frankenstine Doctor to normal scientists of academia, that rest of Rodents are. Also, Rodents are typical as small crafts masters, like seamstress.</li> <li>Rodents have <b>Whisper</b>, instead of <b>Bond</b> or <b>Mystery</b>, for dogs and cats, respectively.</li> <li>Rodents are MAXIMUM the size of Chihuahua or Pomeranians - that is, they are 'Halflings' and 'Dwarves' of Realms of Pugmire. \ud83d\ude09</li> <li>In rodent culture, &quot;shiny&quot; actually means knowledge, due to the writings of Man describing the smartest people as &quot;brilliant\u201d or &quot;illuminated&quot;. Getting \u201cshiny\u201d may got you Fortune points.</li> <li>Rodents create \u2018migration communities\u2019 in other races kingdoms, like Chinatowns in USA.</li> <li>Next <b>Squeaks</b> playtest adventure will be on <b>Onyx Path Con</b> in June.</li> </ul><img src=\"https://scontent-waw1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/176177193_10216342745396134_1147745808643836013_n.jpg?_nc_cat=108&amp;ccb=1-3&amp;_nc_sid=730e14&amp;_nc_ohc=JaoBMeS2vpUAX-iL0UI&amp;_nc_ht=scontent-waw1-1.xx&amp;oh=93c298ed7a9062562bc5987578d3ae1c&amp;oe=60A6271E\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-08-2021, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T20:14:38-07:00","id":1446025,"title":"","content":"On Friday April 30, there will be an entire Pathcast devoted to <b>Squeaks in the Deep</b> - fans of rats and mice will turn their ears! \ud83d\udc2d <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-swiss-cheese-meeting-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/a-swiss-chees...meeting-notes/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T05:40:49-07:00","id":1446276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1445343-realms-of-pugmire-squeaks-in-the-deep#post1445343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Rodents are MAXIMUM the size of Chihuahua or Pomeranians - that is, they are 'Halflings' and 'Dwarves' of Realms of Pugmire. \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but that's inaccurate. <i>Mice </i>are <i>on average </i>about the size of a small dog. Rats are on average a little shorter than the average cat (such as on the cover of Monarchies of Mau). So, there can be dogs (and even cats) smaller than rats. Sorry for the confusion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T07:59:46-07:00","id":1447941,"title":"","content":"Whole lotta new information on <b>Squeaks in the Deep</b> from Pathcast about book!!! \u2764\ud83d\udc2d\u2764 ( Link here - <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/pb-nh9ri-1022430\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.podbean.com/media/share/pb-nh9ri-1022430</a> )<ul><li><b>Inside Extended info about Cult of Labo Tor!</b></li> </ul><b>New Callings</b><br /><br /> <b>Mouse</b><br /><br /><ul><li><b>Psychics</b> \u2013 Psionic focused, but more emotional side, more healing - and body horror</li> <li><b>Rascals </b>\u2013 Very cavalry, Three Musketeers-like, more charming than sneaks. Based on <i>Reepicheep</i> from <b>Chronicles of Narnia</b>. Very <i>Sea Hawk</i> from <b>She-Ra</b>.</li> <li><b>Tricksters </b>\u2013 Traditional rouge mouses. But more witty,</li> </ul><b>Rats</b><br /><br /><ul><li><b>Analysts</b> \u2013 Scientific, very into psionics. Very <i>Entrapta</i> from <b>She-Ra</b>.</li> <li><b>Strategists</b> \u2013 Cunning tacticians. Schemers and plotters. D&amp;D analogue are Warlords.</li> <li><b>Ruffians </b>\u2013 More brawler like rats.</li> </ul><b>Backgrounds</b><br /><br /><ul><li>You CANNOT take <b>Noble</b> Background \u2013 as there are no any Rodent Nobles. ( Side note: Rodents society is very socialist, on general. \ud83d\ude09 There can be 9 Rat Kings at the same time \u2013 but no Nobles. \ud83d\ude1b )</li> <li><b>Deep Dwellers</b> \u2013 You live literally under Monarchies or Pugmire.</li> <li><b>Field Rodents </b>\u2013 Living in \u2018wild\u2019.</li> <li><b>Refugees</b> \u2013 Fled to Monarchies of Pugmire from against violence. Often disillusioned.</li> </ul><b>Underneath</b><br /><br /><ul><li>Underground 'kingdom', analogue to Underdark, but in Realms of Pugmire. Made from network of tunnels and caves stretching out from Pugmire, through Fearful Forest, up to ends of <i>Monarchies</i>. In <b>Monarchies of Mau </b>book there is mentioned about Korat training ground underground, for example. On general, cats and dogs are more likely to go across Fearful Frost than by Underneath, just because it\u2019s so dangerous, unreliable and wild.</li> <li><i>Underneath </i>shape and layout is constantly chaging ( It\u2019s Eddy\u2019s take on MegaDungeons ) Some changes are cause Rodents are building or rebuilding. Part is cause monsters are building and rebuilding. And part is the walls are changing on their own \u2013 no one knows why.</li> <li><b><i>Dungeon Set Pieces</i></b> \u2013 for this book are prepared mini-dungeons with prepared maps for specific theme you can put where you want them, to the <i>Underneath\u2019s \u2018</i>MegaDungeon\u2019 Examples: Cult of Labo Tor hideout, cave with couple of encounters, Rodents villages.</li> <li>Between Set Pieces are <b><i>Tunnels</i></b> creating Underneath \u2013 and they have specific written <b>Tunnels Encounters</b>, that can be Random from tables, any you can put as you like. And between them are villages in Underneath.</li> <li><b>Enemies</b> \u2013 Book is showing new monsters to Realms of Pugmire world that are genuine creepy.</li> <li><b>Cinematic Actions </b>\u2013 Characters can change environment, exterior, setting, just to add variety to dungeons.</li> <li><b>4 Adventures </b>\u2013 3 smaller Adventures and 1 Bigger Adventure, with start in both Pugmire and Monarchies. \ud83d\ude0e</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T05:16:18-07:00","id":1448313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1445343-realms-of-pugmire-squeaks-in-the-deep?p=1447941#post1447941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>4 Adventures </b>\u2013 3 smaller Adventures and 1 Bigger Adventure, with start in both Pugmire and Monarchies. \ud83d\ude0e[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's inaccurate. What was said was that <i>unlike Pirates of Pugmire which had three smaller adventures</i>, Squeaks in the Deep will have one bigger adventure, along with lots of smaller encounters for Guides to mix and match. I highly encourage folks to check out the episode themselves to learn more! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/episode-153-squeaks-in-the-deep-dive-to-the-underneath/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/episode-153-squeaks-in-the-deep-dive-to-the-underneath/\" target=\"_blank\"> Episode 153: Squeaks in the Deep Dive to the Underneath! &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/episode-153-squeaks-in-the-deep-dive-to-the-underneath/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/episode-153-squeaks-in-the-deep-dive-to-the-underneath/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","